window.products.push({"id":1175388,"name":"Eschenbach MaxEvent Binocular Glasses","category":"electronics","retail price":205.8,"sale price":null,"image":"https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/61unBg8O8HL._AC_SL1500_.jpg","description":"Eschenbach MaxEvent Telescopic Glasses With MAXEvent, the easiest-to-fit, binocular distance system, you will be able to see indoor and outdoor events occurring in your daily lives with more crisp and clear vision!   These hands-free, head-mounted glasses provide 2.1x magnification AND can be adjusted so that each eye lens is able to be focused separately [±3 diopters], making the system adaptable to most patients!   The glasses will focus on objects from distances of 3 meters [10 feet] to infinity, and are perfect for viewing sports events, concerts, movies, theater, bird watching, or any other distance viewing activity where a magnified image would be helpful.   The mirrored coating eliminates sun glare and ensures that ‘enlarged eyes’ of the wearer are not visible to the external observer. With flexible temples and rounded edges, MAXEvent telescopic glasses are the most comfortable long-range viewing device ever.   Specifications:   Magnification: 2.1x Lens Size: 32mm Lens Type: Galilean Case Material: Framed nylon with zipper Lens Material: PXM Miscellaneous: Can be adjusted (+/- 3D) for spherical correction Temple Length: 135mm Bridge: Open saddle Frame Size: 137mm Focal Range: 10 feet to infinity Visual Field: 20 degrees PD Range: 60mm - 68mm Weight: 1.7 ounces or 49 grams Rx-able: No   About Eschenbach Optik of America (EOA) Eschenbach Optik of America (EOA) originated in 1983 as the North American branch of Josef Eschenbach's optical products business in Nuremburg, Germany. Eschenbach's business includes an innovative history responsible for products such as injection-molding lenses, an illuminated magnifier, and the aplanatic lens design. Now located in Ridgefield, Connecticut, EOA has Territory Managers and affiliates providing training and top-notch customer support to clients in North, Central, and South America.","images":["https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/61unBg8O8HL._AC_SL1500_.jpg","https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/61zNIJh6ZCL._SL1500_.jpg","https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/61TWUez1VxL._AC_SL1500_.jpg","https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/51TIpnkrEpL._AC_SL1500_.jpg","https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/51I6jTu8yCL._AC_SL1300_.jpg","https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/31o9GyU6jnL._AC_.jpg"],"specifications":{"brand":"Eschenbach Optik","source_asin":"B003DQWWZ4","category_path":"Electronics"},"sku":"BM-1175388","productType":"Electronics","inventory":0,"age_group":"Adult","gender":"Unisex","source_url":"https://www.amazon.com/dp/B003DQWWZ4","source_catalog":"Amazon Reviews 2023 product metadata","source_file":"electronics-range.jsonl","source_asin":"B003DQWWZ4","price_pending":true,"merchant_ready":false});
